erDiagram
    %% This diagram contains only derived/materialized tables.
    %% These are regenerated from source-of-truth tables and are not authoritative raw records.
    %% Source lineage:
    %%  - output_ts is the primary source for all variable summaries.
    %%  - output_grids_repo can contribute to derived grid-level summaries.
    %%  - run_catalog is the authoritative source for run metadata.
    %% Physical design:
    %%  - derived_event_variable_summary: partition bucket(512, event_id), variable; sort event_id, variable, run_type, run_version
    %%  - derived_event_element_variable_summary: partition bucket(512, event_id), variable; sort event_id, element_id, variable, run_type, run_version
    %%  - derived_event_peak_by_variable: partition bucket(512, event_id), variable; sort event_id, variable, run_type, run_version
    %%  - derived_event_element_peak: partition bucket(512, event_id), variable; sort event_id, element_id, variable, run_type, run_version
    %%  - derived_event_model_rollup: partition bucket(512, event_id), variable; sort event_id, model_id, variable, run_type, run_version
    %%  - derived_event_window_rollup: partition bucket(512, event_id), variable; sort event_id, element_id, variable, window_start
    %%  - derived_run_catalog: partition run_type; sort run_type, model_id, started_at
    %%  - derived_latest_run_pointer: partition run_type; sort event_id, model_id, run_type
    %% Freshness and rebuild guidance:
    %%  - Rebuild cadence: per completed run (incremental by run_id) or by run batch...TBD.
    %%  - Late data handling: overwrite/merge by run_id + run_version.
    %%  - Derived tables are safe to fully regenerate when logic changes.

